        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "robot_names = [\"Josh\", \"Hemma\", \"Martin\", \"Josh\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "def find_repeat_values(items):\n",
        "\n",
        "    duplicates = []\n",
        "\n",
        "    # N outer loop iterations\n",
        "    for i, name_a in enumerate(items[:-1]):\n",
        "\n",
        "        # N-i inner loop iterations\n",
        "        for name_b in items[i+1:]:\n",
        "            if (name_a == name_b): \n",
        "                duplicates.append(name_a)\n",
        "\n",
        "    return set(duplicates)\n",
        "\n",
        "find_repeat_values(robot_names)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "8e13129e",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The total number of comparisons forms a triangular number series:\n",
        "\n",
        "$k = (n-1) + (n-2) + ...  + 2 + 1$\n",
        "\n",
        "If we add the series to the same series written in reverse, we get:\n",
        "\n",
        "$2k = n + n + n + ... + n$\n",
        "\n",
        "(There are $n-1$ terms each equal to $n$)\n",
        "\n",
        "So we can simplify the number of comparisons to:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$k = \\frac{n(n-1)}{2} = \\frac{n^2-n}{2}$$"
      ]
    },
