        "Remeber that in Big O notation, **constant multipliers** and **smaller-order** terms are ignored \n",
        "\n",
        "So an algorithm with number of comparisons $k = \\frac{n^2-n}{2}$ has linear complexity $O(n^2)$, as $n^2$ is the dominant term\n",
        "\n"
      ]
